fuel-extractor-slot-name = Container cradle

fuel-extractor-popup-seated = The drill bites into the seep and locks into place.
fuel-extractor-popup-no-seep = The drill grinds against solid rock. There is no seep beneath it.

fuel-extractor-examine-unanchored = It needs to be wrenched down over a seep before it will pump.
fuel-extractor-examine-no-seep = It is anchored over bare rock. Move it onto a seep.
fuel-extractor-examine-dry = The pocket underneath is [color=gray]dry[/color].
fuel-extractor-examine-tapped = It is drawing [color=yellow]{ $fuel }[/color] out of the rock below.
fuel-extractor-examine-buffer-full = Its tank is [color=orange]full[/color], and fuel is spilling onto the floor. Drain it or place a container in the cradle.

fuel-extractor-popup-overflowing = The drill's tank is full! Fuel is spilling onto the floor.

fuel-seep-examine-remaining = The pocket still holds about [color=yellow]{ $percent }%[/color] of its [color=yellow]{ $fuel }[/color].
fuel-seep-examine-dry = The pocket has been pumped [color=gray]dry[/color].
